// Phase 08 Task 1 -- Pattern B (UsesParam), REFUSING member.
// Twin of twin_b_accept.schway: the two members' CALLER body (escort) is
// byte-identical apart from this module header/name (verified by
// TestInterproceduralTwinPairsDifferOnlyInTheCallee). Both members declare
// `fn probe(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer` IDENTICALLY -- every function this
// grammar can express declares `ParameterContract.Mode == "owned"` (there is
// no declared parameter-mode syntax), which is precisely why UsesParam must
// be BODY-derived (D-08-01) and can never come from a declared field the
// way Pattern A's ReturnsBorrowOfParam does. They differ only in probe's
// BODY: here, probe reads its own parameter (`let seen = borrow buffer`)
// before returning an owned value -- deriveFunctionUsesParam counts a plain
// borrow of a parameter-derived place as a genuine use (any operation kind
// other than OpCall/OpReturn), so probe's own `usesParam` bit is true.
//
// caller shape: `borrow; move; call` -- escort borrows buffer, immediately
// takes (moves) buffer, THEN calls probe with the earlier borrow. This is
// the ONE order in which whether the callee reads its own parameter (the
// backward D-08-08 gate) actually determines whether the earlier move was
// premature: 08-02's own synthetic core.Program twin
// (TestInterproceduralLivenessTwinPatternB) already proves, at the checked-
// core level with a REAL interprocedural summary table, that this shape
// refuses exactly when the callee's usesParam is true.
//
// KNOWN LIMITATION (recorded in 08-03-SUMMARY.md's Deviations, out of this
// plan's file scope -- check.go is not in files_modified): run through the
// real ast.Program -> check.Program pipeline, this exact caller shape is
// refused INTRAPROCEDURALLY (ownership.move_while_borrowed), identically for
// BOTH twin_b members, before check's own interprocedural pass ever runs
// (check.Program only reaches checkInterproceduralLoanLiveness once every
// function's own intraprocedural admission has already produced zero
// diagnostics). The cause: computeLoanLastUses (check.go's AST-shadow
// intraprocedural admission path) always calls loanLivenessFixpoint with the
// ZERO-VALUE interproceduralSummaryTable{} -- every summaries.lookup misses,
// so blockLoanLiveness's backward OpCall gate (D-08-08) treats every callee
// as "absent", which counts as usesParam == true (the refusing direction,
// unconditionally) regardless of what the REAL callee actually does. 08-02's
// own SUMMARY flagged this exact residual as an open item for whichever plan
// landed the real .schway fixture pair for this pattern (08-02-SUMMARY.md,
// "Next Phase Readiness"). This fixture pair therefore demonstrates the twin
// discipline (byte-identical caller, callee bodies differing only in
// UsesParam-relevant behavior) and parses/admits identically to its twin at
// the intraprocedural layer; the CONTRACT-DRIVEN differentiation itself is
// proven at the checked-core level by 08-02's own
// TestInterproceduralLivenessTwinPatternB, extended in this plan to ALSO
// exercise these two real fixtures and assert the (identical, intraprocedural)
// verdict they actually produce end to end.

module phase08.twin_b_refuse

export {
  fn escort
}

fn probe(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let seen = borrow buffer
  let taken = take buffer
  taken
}

fn escort(buffer: Buffer) -> Buffer {
  let borrowed = borrow buffer
  let delivered = take buffer
  let observed = probe(borrowed)
  observed
}
